WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:05.640
What's Baylan Skoll up to? Just how&nbsp;
powerful is Ezra? And, most importantly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:10.920
where the heck is Zeb? These are big questions&nbsp;
— and Ahsoka's latest episode holds the answers.

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:16.200
Episode 7 of Ahsoka finally reunites&nbsp;
Ahsoka Tano with Sabine Wren and Ezra&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:21.480
Bridger on Peridea — but the circumstances are&nbsp;
far from ideal. The Jedi's quest to assist her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:26.460
allies in their fight against Baylan Skoll and&nbsp;
Shin Hati has allowed Grand Admiral Thrawn to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:31.380
escape the planet and return to the known galaxy.&nbsp;
Clearly, our heroes are facing an uphill battle.

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:36.240
The latest installment of the Disney+ series&nbsp;
also includes some telling moments of dialogue,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:39.240
adding more depth to certain&nbsp;
characters and addressing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:41.940
fates of others. So what might you have missed?

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:47.760
"A long time ago, in a galaxy far, far away…"

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:53.640
Ahsoka reunites most of the surviving members&nbsp;
of the Ghost crew from Star Wars Rebels,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:57.840
but the current whereabouts of Zeb&nbsp;
was, until now, a mystery. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:02.700
this question is answered when a conversation&nbsp;
between Sabine Wren and Ezra Bridger reveals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:05.940
that he's currently training the next&nbsp;
generation of fighters for the New Republic.

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:11.760
"There's a New Republic, Zeb's training&nbsp;
recruits, and Hera's commanding a fleet."

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:15.900
While there are many Star Wars fans&nbsp;
out there who want to see him join&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:18.900
up with his old comrades again, it's&nbsp;
good to know that he's keeping busy.

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:23.640
Of course, Zeb's current role in the galaxy&nbsp;
far, far away was hinted at in The Mandalorian,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:28.200
as he makes an appearance in that show's&nbsp;
third season. While this is basically a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:32.520
throwaway scene in the grand scheme of things,&nbsp;
it suggests that Zeb will have a bigger role to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:37.860
play in Disney+'s live-action Star Wars output&nbsp;
in the near future. With a war between the New&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:42.720
Republic and Grand Admiral Thrawn seemingly on&nbsp;
the horizon, Ahsoka and the gang will need all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:47.460
of the allies they can find; Zeb's piloting and&nbsp;
combat skills will no doubt be extremely useful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:51.540
to their mission. Fans will agree, of course,&nbsp;
that Zeb's comeback can't come soon enough.

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:54.420
And then there's Baylan&nbsp;
Skoll. Baylan — or, at least,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:58.500
Dave Filoni — is clearly a scholar of&nbsp;
earthling history, as Ahsoka's first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:03.180
season has seen him repeatedly reference quotes&nbsp;
from real-life historical figures. For example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:07.140
Episode 4 sees him pay homage to&nbsp;
Pablo Picasso when he proclaims that:

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:10.800
"One must destroy in order to create."

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:15.540
This quote essentially paraphrases&nbsp;
the great artist's mantra that "every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:19.500
act of creation begins with an act of&nbsp;
destruction" — and it really makes you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.660
wonder what Baylan's grand plan is really about.

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:27.840
Episode 7, meanwhile, sees Baylan directly quote&nbsp;
King Louis XIV when he tells Shin Hati that:

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:34.140
"Impatience for victory will guarantee defeat."

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:38.640
Given that the 17th-century French monarch&nbsp;
enjoyed a 72-year reign on the throne,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:42.600
it's safe to say that he learned a thing&nbsp;
or two about playing the long game. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:46.800
is wise advice to give to an ambitious&nbsp;
warrior who craves power in her own right,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:50.580
and it says a lot about Baylan's&nbsp;
mindset heading into the upcoming war.

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:54.780
But what do these historical quotes&nbsp;
mean for the former Jedi? For one thing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:58.620
they clearly show that he's willing to be&nbsp;
patient before initiating his secret master&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:03.660
plan. We already know that Baylan wants Thrawn&nbsp;
to start a war, presumably so he can rebuild&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:09.120
the galaxy from the ashes afterward. However, his&nbsp;
words to Shin in Episode 7 highlight the fact he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:14.100
doesn't expect change to happen overnight — and&nbsp;
that he's probably harboring ulterior motives.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:18.240
Back on the side of the angels, Ahsoka's&nbsp;
seventh episode displays Ezra Bridger's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:23.040
new status as a full-on Force ninja — one who&nbsp;
doesn't need lightsabers or blasters to help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:26.880
him win a fight. In the fight against&nbsp;
Shin and her minions, he tells Sabine:

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:30.900
"The Force is my ally. That's all I need."

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:35.400
After this, he defeats their foes using both&nbsp;
the Force and some good ol' fashioned brawling.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:39.600
What's more, Ezra manages to block one of&nbsp;
Shin's lightsaber attacks with his mind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:43.980
which is a rare accomplishment even for&nbsp;
the most skilled Force wielders. That said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:47.880
Ezra isn't the first person to pull it&nbsp;
off; Darth Vader does the same to Reva&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:52.020
in Obi-Wan Kenobi when she tries to attack&nbsp;
him from behind with her own lightsaber.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:55.620
Kylo Ren and Rey also master the&nbsp;
trick in The Rise of Skywalker.

00:03:55.620 --> 00:04:00.120
This moment essentially confirms that Ezra&nbsp;
has mastered the ways of the Force — and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:03.676
that he's nearly as formidable as some of&nbsp;
the most powerful beings in the galaxy.

